WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.648 --> 00:00:03.798
- [Narrator] These are nachos.

00:00:03.798 --> 00:00:06.829
Golden crispy chips, gooey melted cheese,

00:00:06.829 --> 00:00:09.175
mounds of toppings galore.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.357
They are delicious.

00:00:11.357 --> 00:00:13.185
They're named after a man,

00:00:13.185 --> 00:00:14.685
a man named Nacho.

00:00:18.872 --> 00:00:20.961
This was Ignacio Anaya,

00:00:20.961 --> 00:00:23.795
known to friends and foes alike as Nacho.

00:00:23.795 --> 00:00:27.171
In 1943, Ignacio was a
maître d' at this restaurant,

00:00:27.171 --> 00:00:30.081
The Old Victory Club, in
Piedras Negras, Mexico,

00:00:30.081 --> 00:00:32.075
a border town a jalapeño's throw

00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:34.927
from Eagle Pass, Texas,
home of Fort Duncan,

00:00:34.927 --> 00:00:38.041
an army base filled with
military men and families.

00:00:38.041 --> 00:00:40.402
One day, a group of army
wives crossed the border,

00:00:40.402 --> 00:00:42.277
they shopped, they got hungry,

00:00:42.277 --> 00:00:44.872
they went to The Victory Club.

00:00:44.872 --> 00:00:46.705
The chef wasn't there.

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:51.626
But Ignacio, maître d', didn't
want to turn the women away,

00:00:51.626 --> 00:00:53.608
so he sprang into action.

00:00:53.608 --> 00:00:56.370
Grabbing tortillas,
shredded cheddar cheese

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:00.090
and jalapeños, he put his
creation into the oven.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.379
Pensively, he served it to the army wives.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:03.546
They loved it.

00:01:05.011 --> 00:01:08.929
Returning to Texas, they spread
the el evangelio del nacho,

00:01:08.929 --> 00:01:10.789
the gospel of the nacho.

00:01:10.789 --> 00:01:13.942
Nachos especialios became
so adored and renowned

00:01:13.942 --> 00:01:15.896
Ignacio opened up his own restaurant,

00:01:15.896 --> 00:01:19.396
the creatively named Nacho's Restaurante.

